1
00:00:02,100 --> 00:00:06,400
Robbie, this new Walkman is absolutely wonderful.

2
00:00:06,400 --> 00:00:10,200
Richard and Marilyn bought it for me for my birthday.

3
00:00:10,200 --> 00:00:12,300
They're so thoughtful.

4
00:00:12,300 --> 00:00:17,900
You are very lucky, Robbie, to have such a nice family.

5
00:00:17,900 --> 00:00:19,600
Is something wrong, Alexandra?

6
00:00:19,600 --> 00:00:22,500
No, nothing.

7
00:00:22,500 --> 00:00:23,700
Yes, there is.

8
00:00:23,700 --> 00:00:25,900
I can tell.

9
00:00:25,900 --> 00:00:27,700
What's the matter?

10
00:00:27,700 --> 00:00:30,600
Come on, you can tell me.

11
00:00:30,600 --> 00:00:32,260
What's up?

12
00:00:32,260 --> 00:00:34,800
I don't know.

13
00:00:34,800 --> 00:00:38,900
Something's wrong.

14
00:00:38,900 --> 00:00:43,800
OK, let's talk.

15
00:00:43,800 --> 00:00:47,300
I received a letter from my parents this morning.

16
00:00:47,300 --> 00:00:49,400
Did they write some bad news?

17
00:00:49,400 --> 00:00:51,200
No.

18
00:00:51,200 --> 00:00:53,900
Well, then why are you so sad?

19
00:00:53,900 --> 00:00:55,000
I miss them.

20
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:57,900
I miss them very much.

21
00:00:57,900 --> 00:01:01,300
I'm sorry, Alexandra.

22
00:01:01,300 --> 00:01:05,300
But I understand.

23
00:01:05,300 --> 00:01:07,900
The Molinas treat me so nicely,

24
00:01:07,900 --> 00:01:13,100
and I love being with your family so much ...

25
00:01:13,100 --> 00:01:14,300
but when I received the letter

26
00:01:14,300 --> 00:01:18,700
with photographs of my family, I cried.

27
00:01:18,700 --> 00:01:21,200
I cried because I miss them all.

28
00:01:21,200 --> 00:01:23,300
You really miss your family, don't you?

29
00:01:23,300 --> 00:01:28,900
Yes. I know I must seem silly.

30
00:01:28,900 --> 00:01:31,500
It's not like I have nobody.

31
00:01:31,500 --> 00:01:33,700
I like the Molinas very much,

32
00:01:33,700 --> 00:01:40,600
and they're so kind to me.

33
00:01:40,600 --> 00:01:41,900
Hey, why don't we go out

34
00:01:41,900 --> 00:01:43,900
for a cheeseburger and french fries?

35
00:01:43,900 --> 00:01:45,800
That'll cheer you up.

36
00:01:45,800 --> 00:01:49,400
And you can use my Walkman.

37
00:01:49,400 --> 00:01:51,800
That's a good idea.

38
00:01:51,800 --> 00:01:54,000
But if we go out,

39
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:56,960
please don't complain

40
00:01:56,960 --> 00:02:00,000
about your math teacher or your math homework.

41
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:01,500
I want to have fun.

42
00:02:01,500 --> 00:02:03,200
So do I.

43
00:02:03,200 --> 00:02:04,500
I have to turn off the lights,

44
00:02:04,500 --> 00:02:07,100
or else my father will get really angry.

45
00:02:07,100 --> 00:02:10,500
He says I never turn them out when I leave.

46
00:02:10,500 --> 00:02:16,200
If they come home and they're on ...

47
00:02:16,200 --> 00:02:17,700
Do you hear something?

48
00:02:17,700 --> 00:02:18,000
Yes.

49
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:20,600
What was that?

50
00:02:20,600 --> 00:02:23,200
It sounded like a dog barking.

51
00:02:23,200 --> 00:02:25,600
It sounded like a dog barking right here.

52
00:02:25,600 --> 00:02:29,800
Yeah.

53
00:02:29,800 --> 00:02:30,900
A dog!

54
00:02:30,900 --> 00:02:35,000
A springer spaniel!

55
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:35,580
Come on in!

56
00:02:35,580 --> 00:02:37,500
Make yourself at home.

57
00:02:37,500 --> 00:02:41,100
Oh, you poor little thing.

58
00:02:41,100 --> 00:02:50,300
Come on.

59
00:02:50,300 --> 00:02:52,500
Poor baby.

60
00:02:52,500 --> 00:02:58,100
Where did you come from?

61
00:02:58,100 --> 00:03:00,100
Her name's Gemma,

62
00:03:00,100 --> 00:03:03,400
and she belongs to Mr. and Mrs. Levinson.

63
00:03:03,400 --> 00:03:05,600
There's a phone number --

64
00:03:05,600 --> 00:03:10,400
five five five ... eight four four eight.

65
00:03:10,400 --> 00:03:12,800
Robbie, maybe you should call them

66
00:03:12,800 --> 00:03:16,400
and tell the Levinsons we have their cute little spaniel.

67
00:03:16,400 --> 00:03:18,500
I've always wanted a springer spaniel.

68
00:03:18,500 --> 00:03:37,000
She's so cute.

69
00:03:37,000 --> 00:03:43,300
The number you are calling -- 555-8448 --

70
00:03:43,300 --> 00:03:48,100
is no longer in service.

71
00:03:48,100 --> 00:03:53,100
The number's no longer in service.

72
00:03:53,100 --> 00:03:55,400
Oh, you poor, poor baby.

73
00:03:55,400 --> 00:03:58,100
You've lost your family.

74
00:03:58,100 --> 00:03:58,400
We'll find them.

75
00:03:58,400 --> 00:04:01,400
Don't worry, Alexandra.
